It depends on what you use your stash for.  If you
are building an ascension kit then closer to the
top is good.  If you're building a descent kit then
a small stash with several alternates for each
type of item is great to bring to a level above
your deepest.  If you're a packrat who wants to
keep every item in the dungeon in your stash, it's
too big to carry around constantly.  So to me it
makes sense to have a small stash shallow with items
I intend to take into the planes and that I will not
use until then, plus a small stash with the best
alternate tools, armor and weapons that I carry
down to keep near me, plus maybe a centrally
located huge hoard of packrat junk for potential
polypiling.

